00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.320
We all heard about Shohar Rukh, yes, and we heard also about the Mishti Tora.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:18.400
What I want to show today is that there is a radical, basic, structural difference between

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.480
Shohar Rukh and Hanbal.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:29.040
And this will explain why the Shohar Rukh is so popular.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:38.680
We know that the Maran wrote actually two books, Debate Yourself, in which he discusses,

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:45.919
argues the different views, and argues them from a Halakha point of view, which is fantastic.

00:00:45.919 --> 00:00:53.439
It's a great new way to look into Halakha, to take different views, and to analyze them,

00:00:53.439 --> 00:00:58.439
to give credence to all the views, and then after analysis to say more or less which one

00:00:58.439 --> 00:01:01.840
is the more appropriate one.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.000
But then you have the Shohar Rukh.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:13.000
And when we read the Shohar Rukh, we assume that we're reading a text.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.400
No, it's not a text.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.040
It's a collection of titles.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:34.120
Every word is the title of a subject that is yet to be determined by a Posek or many

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.120
Posekim.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:42.519
In other words, you read a Shohar Rukh, these are not words, yes, in which you could join

00:01:42.519 --> 00:01:45.800
the words to a sentence, no.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:53.680
These are little windows, and the Posek sees these windows, and this is the point of which

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:58.000
I think is so important, and sometimes we neglect to do this.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:05.080
And therefore the Posek, according to the situation at hand, he could, I don't like

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:10.919
the word manipulate, but could determine the Halakha, according to the customs, to this,

00:02:10.919 --> 00:02:11.919
to that.

00:02:11.919 --> 00:02:14.039
In other words, it's not Mishne Tora.

00:02:14.279 --> 00:02:21.559
Mishne Tora, you have one view, the view of Aram Bam, and the purpose of the Mishneh

00:02:21.559 --> 00:02:25.279
Tora is to instruct, instruct you.

00:02:25.279 --> 00:02:28.279
And separate, no, separate, this is a different point.

00:02:28.279 --> 00:02:34.399
Yeah, Maran, that's what I want to show, it's not to instruct somebody who is unlearned,

00:02:34.399 --> 00:02:44.000
yes, but it's rather to offer windows, windows, and not more than windows, yes.

00:02:44.119 --> 00:02:47.119
To the Posek.

00:02:47.119 --> 00:02:52.559
And this is what made the Shohar Arukh such an extraordinary book.

